From e1b722bcb00cee73dbcfc1c48a9780b653eb7ad7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greg Hudson <ghudson@mit.edu>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:07:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 67/89] Prevent null deref in KDC dispatch corner case

If a KDC request matches an entry in the lookaside cache, we transmit
the reply without decoding the request, and therefore without looking
up the applicable realm.  But if the cached reply is longer than
kdc_max_dgram_reply_size, we need the applicable realm's TGS server
principal to construct a KRB_ERR_RESPONSE_TOO_BIG KRB-ERROR message.
Currently this results in a null derefernce.  This case is unlikely to
happen with the default kdc_max_dgram_reply_size value of 65536, but
may be triggerable by an unauthenticated attacker if the value is
lowered.  Prevent a null dereference in this scenario by setting an
initial guess at the realm before checking the lookaside cache.
Reported by AWS Security.

ticket: 9238 (new)
tags: pullup
target_version: 1.22-next

(cherry picked from commit 774506e972dea98e0cd770109b0af89473ebe21d)
---
 src/kdc/dispatch.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kdc/dispatch.c b/src/kdc/dispatch.c
index 28def3be47..1caafde1e7 100644
--- a/src/kdc/dispatch.c
+++ b/src/kdc/dispatch.c
@@ -109,6 +109,10 @@ dispatch(void *cb, const krb5_fulladdr *local_addr,
     state->is_tcp = is_tcp;
     state->kdc_err_context = kdc_err_context;
 
+    /* Start with a guess at the applicable realm, in case we need one to
+     * produce an error message without having decoded the request. */
+    state->active_realm = handle->kdc_realmlist[0];
+
     /* decode incoming packet, and dispatch */
 
 #ifndef NOCACHE
